content.body:
About the `export * from` refactoring hazard, to be clear it's this:
```js
// entry.js
export * from "a.js";
export * from "b.js";

// a.js
export let a = 1;
export default 2;

// b.js
export let b = 3;
```
with this proposal `entry.js` would export `a`, `default`, and `b`.

If `b.js` adds a default export, then `entrty.js` will only export `a` and `b`. This is the same as if `b.js` added an `a` export, then `entry.js` will stop exporting `a`.

It is true that adding a `default` export is more likely than adding a `a` export, but it's also something that will be caught very easily
